@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] no-secret-logging
Credentials, access/refresh tokens, authorization headers, and request bodies (full prompts) MUST NOT be logged or emitted in errors, spans, or the request ring buffer.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] credential-storage
OAuth credentials and minted keys MUST be persisted only to the underclass SQLite store or the opencode auth.json written by `underclass connect`; auth.json MUST be created/updated with 0600 permissions. Credentials and pool.db MUST NOT be committed to the repository.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:logging] identity-formatting
Account identity in logs and the request ring buffer MUST use the account label (email/username) in full; raw UUID account IDs MUST be truncated to their first 8 characters. `src/logging.rs` is the only place that formats identity for logs.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:architecture] pure-sync-core
`src/pool.rs` and `src/health.rs` MUST remain pure and synchronous: no tokio, no I/O, no wall-clock access — time enters as an injected `now_ms` parameter. Property tests in `tests/properties.rs` depend on this.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:proxy] pre-output-failover
Failover across pool accounts MUST happen only before any response byte has been sent to the client. A streamed 2xx response MAY be held back until its first model-output or terminal event (bounded in time and bytes) and retried on another account only when that terminal event is a capacity failure (`is_overload_code`) with no output before it. Once any byte has been sent to the client, upstream errors MUST pass through and MUST NOT be retried on another account.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:architecture] backend-agnostic-core
Pool routing, health classification, and stickiness MUST NOT special-case any backend by name; all backend differences MUST live behind `provider::Backend` implementations registered in the backend map.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:proxy] outbound-credential-stripping
Outbound upstream requests MUST carry only proxy-injected credentials (the selected account's token); client-supplied authorization headers MUST NOT be forwarded upstream.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:cli] nix-monitor-command
The flake's underclass package MUST put `underclass` and `utop` in `bin`; `utop` MUST invoke `underclass top` with all user arguments preserved.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:persistence] health-write-under-pool-lock
A write that persists an account's `status`, `reset_at`, or `scope_cooling` MUST be performed while the lock guarding the corresponding `PoolCore` is held, and MUST use the pool's current account rather than a snapshot taken outside that lock; otherwise a concurrent transition can be overwritten in the store and resurrected by `sync_from_store`.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:proxy] unknown-limits-not-zero
`GET /v1/models` MUST emit `context_window`, `max_input_tokens`, and `max_output_tokens` on every entry, as JSON `null` when no source has published the value (the stored `0`) and as the number otherwise, so a client can tell "unknown" from "zero capacity". A key MUST NOT be dropped to express unknown. An alias MUST take each limit as the widest value its servable concretes published, and MUST be `null` only when none of them published one. An alias MUST advertise `scope` only when every servable concrete agrees on one non-empty scope.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:pool] input-falls-back-to-context
When a source publishes a context window but omits its input limit, ingest MUST record `input = context`: absence of `limit.input` means "input equals context", not zero. `input` MUST stay `0` only when no source has published either value.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:proxy] deprecated-never-advertised
A catalog row whose recorded `status` is `deprecated` MUST NOT appear in `GET /v1/models`, MUST NOT keep an alias advertised, MUST NOT contribute to an alias's advertised limits, and MUST NOT be offered to a client by the UI snippet or `underclass connect`'s provider block. The row MUST stay stored and MUST stay visible in `GET /admin/api/catalog/{backend}`, and retirement MUST be recorded on the row rather than held in a hard-coded deny-list.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:pool] metadata-never-invented
A capability, modality, price, effort ladder, knowledge date, or surface name MUST be recorded only when the backend published it. A model that reports reasoning support without an effort array MUST keep an empty ladder, a source that omits a field MUST leave that field absent in `ModelInfo::metadata`, and a surface name this build does not recognise MUST NOT be mapped onto one it does.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:pool] models-dev-failure-is-not-regression
A models.dev read MUST be an enrichment, never a set source and never a regression: on any failure (network, non-2xx, malformed body, or a body without the provider read) the stored catalog and every row in it MUST be left exactly as they were, and the seed table, the backend listing, and the recommended-models feed MUST keep describing the catalog on their own. A models.dev `deprecated` marking MUST NOT retire a model on its own.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:persistence] catalog-metadata-round-trips
The catalog MUST store a model's metadata block in one `catalog.metadata` JSON column added through the idempotent migration pattern, MUST deserialize a row whose metadata is absent or malformed into the empty block rather than dropping the row, MUST round-trip the block through `Store::catalog`/`Store::set_catalog`, and MUST serialize it deterministically so re-writing identical rows is byte-stable.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:pool] catalog-refresh-is-operator-driven
The Cline, OpenCode Go, and Copilot model sets MUST change only on an operator-initiated refresh - the admin catalog refresh endpoints, account onboarding, or a catalog edit - and startup MUST NOT fetch any of those three catalogs, so a restart never changes what the pool advertises and never delays readiness on a catalog read. The Claude catalog MAY refresh at boot, because the dashboard has no Claude refresh endpoint. This replaces the `cline-catalog-refreshed-on-boot` and `opencode-go-catalog-refreshed-on-boot` contracts, which required exactly that boot refresh and were removed with the functions they annotated.
